;; Composition-lane devcard inventory — the authored-lane companion to the
;; atomic corpus/spec.edn.
;;
;; Cards are DATA: each names a devcards.legos maker + its options + an
;; absolute placement; the runner materializes the node (lego fn -> node map,
;; assoc :x/:y) and compiles it through devcards.fixtures/build-authored-card
;; (the ONE gate into events / absolute position / part-selector styling).
;; The atomic lane never admits these cards; the authored lane never admits
;; an atomic card's implicit-theme claim — a composition card proves the
;; PUBLIC LEGO contract (geometry, palette, event identities), not a theme
;; surface.
;;
;; :expect legend (composition lane):
;;   :composition — rendered + invariant-judged (zero findings, zero
;;     render-time emissions) + golden-hashed per dark/light; interaction
;;     probes assert the lego's host-event identities.
;;   :inert-prop  — a prop-inertness pin: byte-identical raw FB to :base-card
;;     (the named sibling); proves an interaction-only prop moves ZERO pixels.
;;     Built by the declared :transform, never by a lego contract fork.
;;
;; :transform legend:
;;   :strip-seek-on-press — dissoc :seek_on_press from the scrubber slider's
;;     slider_props after the lego builds the node (the lego itself sets the
;;     prop unconditionally — press-seek is the scrubber CONTRACT, so the
;;     prop-absent shape exists only as this declared corpus surgery).
;;   :strip-hit-slop — dissoc :hit-slop from the scrubber slider node, same
;;     shape and same reason. Separate from the above because the two used to
;;     be ONE fused flag: one card stripping both could not tell which of the
;;     two is the pixel-inert one, and now each can be varied alone.
;;
;; Scrubber placement arithmetic: :placement positions the lego's HIT-HALO
;; WRAPPER (devcards.legos/scrubber-halo = 24px per side); the TRACK rect
;; lands at placement + halo. The three scrubber cards place at (76,176) so
;; the track sits at (100,200) — the runner's coords check pins this.
{:builder "devcards.fixtures/build-authored-card over devcards.legos makers"
 :canvas {:h 480 :w 800}
 :cards
 [{:expect :composition
   :id "lego/scrubber"
   :lego :scrubber
   :notes
   "Buffered media scrubber: bar underlay (track + buffered band) beneath a transparent-MAIN slider overlay (played band + knob). seek_on_press rides the lego contract; interaction probes assert press-seek [value] with NO duplicate at release, drag prepends exactly one immediate value, and the 24px ext-click envelope (both engines)."
   :opts
   {:buffered 85 :height 20 :max 100 :min 0 :seek-event-name "seek" :value 40 :width 600}
   :placement {:x 76 :y 176}}
  {:expect :composition
   :id "lego/scrubber-plain"
   :lego :scrubber
   :notes
   "No :buffered — a single styled slider (MAIN is the track); no bar underlay in the DOM."
   :opts {:height 20 :max 100 :min 0 :seek-event-name "seek" :value 40 :width 600}
   :placement {:x 76 :y 176}}
  {:base-card "lego/scrubber"
   :expect :inert-prop
   :id "lego/scrubber-noseek"
   :lego :scrubber
   :notes
   "seek_on_press pixel-inertness pin: raw FB must equal lego/scrubber byte-for-byte in both dark and light — the corpus-level restatement of the prop-absent parity proof (the prop changes hit behavior only, never pixels), held per re-mint."
   :opts
   {:buffered 85 :height 20 :max 100 :min 0 :seek-event-name "seek" :value 40 :width 600}
   :placement {:x 76 :y 176}
   :transform :strip-seek-on-press}
  {:base-card "lego/scrubber"
   :expect :inert-prop
   :id "lego/scrubber-noslop"
   :lego :scrubber
   :notes
   "hit_slop pixel-inertness pin: raw FB must equal lego/scrubber byte-for-byte in both dark and light. WidgetNode.hit_slop grows the HIT box only — ext_click_pad is read by lv_obj_get_click_area and by the two dead ADV_HITTEST handlers, and by nothing that draws — so a widened tap target must move zero pixels. The sibling pin above does the same for seek_on_press; the two are separate cards because the props used to be one fused flag."
   :opts
   {:buffered 85 :height 20 :max 100 :min 0 :seek-event-name "seek" :value 40 :width 600}
   :placement {:x 76 :y 176}
   :transform :strip-hit-slop}
  {:expect :composition
   :id "lego/scrubber-rich-full"
   :lego :scrubber-rich
   :notes
   "Every optional part enabled: transport row FLANKED by the elapsed/total readout, the plain scrubber embedded unchanged (halo + press-seek intact), and a labelled tick ruler. Major-tick texts ride ScaleProps.text_src, so the timecode ruler needs no vocabulary beyond WIDGET_SCALE. :playing? true, so the one play/pause button shows the PAUSE glyph."
   :opts
   {:buffered 85
    :height 20
    :labels ["0:00" "0:45" "1:30" "2:15" "3:00"]
    :max 100
    :min 0
    :playing? true
    :readout {:elapsed "1:12" :total "3:00"}
    :seek-event-name "seek"
    :ticks {:major-every 10 :total 41}
    :transport [:prev :play-pause :stop :next]
    :transport-event-name "tp"
    :value 40
    :width 600}
   :placement {:x 76 :y 60}}
  {:expect :composition
   :id "lego/scrubber-rich-paused"
   :lego :scrubber-rich
   :notes
   "The :playing? twin of lego/scrubber-rich-full — identical in every other option, so the ONLY difference between the two renders is the play/pause button's glyph. That is the whole claim of the single stateful transport control: one button, one event identity (tp-play-pause), two icons."
   :opts
   {:buffered 85
    :height 20
    :labels ["0:00" "0:45" "1:30" "2:15" "3:00"]
    :max 100
    :min 0
    :playing? false
    :readout {:elapsed "1:12" :total "3:00"}
    :seek-event-name "seek"
    :ticks {:major-every 10 :total 41}
    :transport [:prev :play-pause :stop :next]
    :transport-event-name "tp"
    :value 40
    :width 600}
   :placement {:x 76 :y 60}}
  {:expect :composition
   :id "lego/scrubber-rich-ticks"
   :lego :scrubber-rich
   :notes
   "Ticks + labels only — no transport, no readout. The additive floor: the same lego with one optional key set is a timecode ruler and nothing more."
   :opts
   {:buffered 85
    :height 20
    :labels ["0:00" "1:30" "3:00"]
    :max 100
    :min 0
    :seek-event-name "seek"
    :ticks {:major-every 20 :total 41}
    :value 40
    :width 600}
   :placement {:x 76 :y 300}}
  {:expect :composition
   :id "lego/dock-expanded"
   :lego :dock-panel
   :notes
   "The three-caption-state floor (enabled+expanded / enabled+collapsed / disabled+expanded). Interaction probes assert the event identities <stage-id>-up/-down/-delete/-toggle (int_value = stage index) and dock-fold."
   :opts
   {:badge 3
    :folded? false
    :stages
    [{:body-nodes [{:props {:w 74} :text "amount" :type :WIDGET_LABEL}
                   {:props {:slider_props {:max_value 100 :min_value 0 :value 60} :w 150}
                    :type :WIDGET_SLIDER}]
      :enabled? true
      :id "blur"
      :label "Blur"}
     {:body-nodes [{:props {:w 74} :text "amount" :type :WIDGET_LABEL}]
      :collapsed? true
      :enabled? true
      :id "sharpen"
      :label "Sharpen"}
     {:body-nodes [{:props {:w 74} :text "amount" :type :WIDGET_LABEL}
                   {:props {:slider_props {:max_value 100 :min_value 0 :value 35} :w 150}
                    :type :WIDGET_SLIDER}]
      :enabled? false
      :id "lut"
      :label "LUT"}]}
   :placement {:x 12 :y 3}}
  {:expect :composition
   :id "lego/dock-multirow"
   :lego :dock-panel
   :notes
   "Multiple body ROWS per stage container. :body-nodes accepts a vector of vectors — one row each — and the card's height is DERIVED from the row count, so a two-row stage grows its container instead of being clipped by a fixed :card-expanded-h. Row content is centred on both axes, so a short row reads as centred in the card rather than pinned to the top-left."
   :opts
   {:badge 2
    :folded? false
    :stages
    [{:body-nodes [[{:props {:w 74} :text "amount" :type :WIDGET_LABEL}
                    {:props {:slider_props {:max_value 100 :min_value 0 :value 60} :w 130}
                     :type :WIDGET_SLIDER}]
                   [{:props {:w 74} :text "radius" :type :WIDGET_LABEL}
                    {:props {:slider_props {:max_value 100 :min_value 0 :value 25} :w 130}
                     :type :WIDGET_SLIDER}]]
      :enabled? true
      :id "blur"
      :label "Blur"}
     {:body-nodes [{:props {:w 74} :text "amount" :type :WIDGET_LABEL}
                   {:props {:slider_props {:max_value 100 :min_value 0 :value 35} :w 130}
                    :type :WIDGET_SLIDER}]
      :enabled? false
      :id "lut"
      :label "LUT"}]}
   :placement {:x 12 :y 3}}
  {:expect :composition
   :id "lego/dock-folded"
   :lego :dock-panel
   :notes
   "The folded icon rail (fold toggle + per-stage letter buttons + badge); only dock-fold is a live identity — rail taps are consumer-side by the ratified shape."
   :opts {:badge 3
          :folded? true
          :stages [{:enabled? true :id "blur" :label "Blur"}
                   {:enabled? true :id "sharpen" :label "Sharpen"}
                   {:enabled? false :id "lut" :label "LUT"}]}
   :placement {:x 12 :y 3}}
  {:expect :composition
   :id "lego/dock-hidden-child"
   :lego :dock-panel
   :notes
   "The corpus subject for the invariant lane's HIDDEN-node designed-geometry exemption. The stage body is ONE unsized WIDGET_LABEL (lv_label's class defaults are LV_SIZE_CONTENT on both axes) carrying a hidden 210x96 WIDGET_OBJ child. LVGL skips a hidden child in calc_content_width/height, so the label sizes to its text and never grows to fit it; the child is not layout-positioned either, so it self-places at the label's content origin at its own size and overhangs the content box obj_clipped measures against. The dump therefore carries :clipped (plus vis_px 0) on a node whose geometry LVGL declares meaningless — exactly the shape devcards.invariants/designed-flag? exempts, now proven end-to-end through a real render instead of unit tests alone. Sized to stay inside the 800x480 canvas because :offscreen is deliberately NOT exempt."
   :opts
   {:badge 1
    :folded? false
    :stages
    [{:body-nodes [{:children [{:flags [:hidden]
                                :props {:h 96 :w 210}
                                :type :WIDGET_OBJ}]
                    :text "hidden"
                    :type :WIDGET_LABEL}]
      :enabled? true
      :id "blur"
      :label "Blur"}]}
   :placement {:x 12 :y 3}}]
 :lane :authored-composition}